# ================================================================
# GitHub Streak Keeper - Ejemplo de Cron Job
# ================================================================
# 
# Instrucciones:
# 1. Abre el crontab: crontab -e
# 2. Copia y pega las líneas de abajo
# 3. Ajusta la ruta del script si es necesario
# 4. Guarda y sale
#
# Verificar instalación: crontab -l
# ================================================================

# GitHub Streak Keeper - 6 commits diarios distribuidos
# Horarios: 8am, 10am, 12pm, 2pm, 4pm, 6pm (hora local)

0 8 * * * /home/carlosdev/proyectos/github-streak-keeper/auto-commit.sh >> /tmp/streak-keeper.log 2>&1
0 10 * * * /home/carlosdev/proyectos/github-streak-keeper/auto-commit.sh >> /tmp/streak-keeper.log 2>&1
0 12 * * * /home/carlosdev/proyectos/github-streak-keeper/auto-commit.sh >> /tmp/streak-keeper.log 2>&1
0 14 * * * /home/carlosdev/proyectos/github-streak-keeper/auto-commit.sh >> /tmp/streak-keeper.log 2>&1
0 16 * * * /home/carlosdev/proyectos/github-streak-keeper/auto-commit.sh >> /tmp/streak-keeper.log 2>&1
0 18 * * * /home/carlosdev/proyectos/github-streak-keeper/auto-commit.sh >> /tmp/streak-keeper.log 2>&1

# ================================================================
# COMANDOS ÚTILES
# ================================================================
#
# Ver logs en tiempo real:
#   tail -f /tmp/streak-keeper.log
#
# Ver últimas 20 líneas:
#   tail -n 20 /tmp/streak-keeper.log
#
# Ver crontab actual:
#   crontab -l
#
# Editar crontab:
#   crontab -e
#
# Eliminar todas las jobs:
#   crontab -r
#
# ================================================================
